.\" Manual page for lion-greeter (spec 01 §9 deliverable).
.\" roff source; install as /usr/share/man/man8/lion-greeter.8
.TH LION-GREETER 8 "2026" "LionOS" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
lion-greeter \- LionOS login backend: user enumeration, PAM authentication, session launch
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lion-greeter
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B lion-greeter
is the privileged login backend of LionOS (spec 01). It owns user
enumeration, PAM authentication and session launch. It never draws
anything; the unprivileged \fIlion-login-ui\fR component renders the
greeter and talks to the daemon over a
.BR SO_PEERCRED Ns -gated
local unix socket (\fI/run/lion-greeter/ui.sock\fR) using a versioned
JSON-lines protocol (proto 1). See
.BR docs/PROTOCOL.md (in the source package)
for the wire format.
.PP
The daemon speaks PAM through a runtime-loaded \fIlibpam\fR and
supports full conversations: passwords, expired-password change flows,
multi-step prompts (OTP/TOTP), and faillock-style lock-outs surfaced to
the UI as countdowns. Secrets are zeroized immediately after use and are
never logged or serialized.
.PP
Successful authentication registers a
.BR logind (1)
session and execs
.BR lion-session (1)
as the user with a clean XDG environment. Guest sessions run from a
tmpfs home. Autologin and timed login are configuration-driven and
fail closed unless the dedicated PAM stack permits them.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIPATH\fR
Configuration file (default \fI/etc/lion/greeter.json\fR; the
.B LION_GREETER_CONFIG
environment variable is honoured).
.TP
.B \-\-check-config
Load and validate the configuration, verify the PAM backend loads, and
exit non-zero on any problem.
.TP
.B \-\-print-schema
Print the lion-config JSON schema shipped with the package.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Debug logging.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGTERM
Graceful shutdown: \fBSTOPPING=1\fR notification, active authentication
aborted and wiped, socket removed.
.TP
.B SIGHUP
Reload configuration atomically without dropping connected clients.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B LION_GREETER_LOG
tracing filter (default \fIinfo\fR).
.TP
.B NOTIFY_SOCKET, WATCHDOG_USEC, LISTEN_FDS
consumed per \fBsd_notify\fR(3) and \fBsd_listen_fds\fR(3) under systemd.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/lion/greeter.json
Configuration.
.TP
.I /run/lion-greeter/ui.sock
UI protocol socket (mode 0660, group \fIlion-greeter\fR).
.TP
.I /var/lib/lion-greeter/last-session/
Per-user remembered session choice.
.TP
.I /etc/pam.d/lion-greeter
PAM stack for password conversations.
.TP
.I /etc/pam.d/lion-greeter-autologin
PAM stack gating autologin (lion-autologin group).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lionctl (1),
.BR lion-session (1),
.BR systemd (1),
.BR pam (8),
.BR pam_faillock (8)
.SH BUGS
Report bugs at the LionOS tracker: https://git.lionos.org/lion-greeter
